Hi All,

I'm trying to use gdistsamp to model density of small prey along transects. I have 5 survey periods that I would like to include as yearlySiteCovs to estimate survey-specific phi, and a lot of missing data because many sites were not sampled all 5 times. Initially I was using the command "formatDistData" to convert my data into the format required for gdistsamp. My models all ran fine and a half-normal key function best fit the data. However, I didn't realize that all of the NAs in my data were being converted to 0s when I used formatDistData, making it look like I had surveyed way more sights than I had, and that I had found nothing. I think I have my data entered correctly now,  with the NAs, but now the only model I can get to run is an exponential key function, which is not recommended in distance modeling. Half-normal and hazard rate functions both give me errors. I've tried using starting values from the exponential function in the other two, but I get the same errors.  Does anyone have any ideas why my models won't run with the NAs added? I'm just trying null models, by the way, with no covariates at all. A summary of my data and the errors I get are below.

Thanks so much for your help!
Lucretia

